<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="band faq-band" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head center rv">
      <h2 class="display">Common questions</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq rv">
      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary>What do I need to do to get started?</summary>
        <p>Sign up with your email, fill in a short profile (your name, your income, and how much risk you are comfortable with), then connect your accounts.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Which accounts can I connect?</summary>
        <p>Banks, credit cards, brokerages, retirement accounts and loans at US institutions, through Plaid. For a house, enter the address and LasagnaFi looks up a value estimate for it, or enter your own figure and it keeps that instead. If no estimate comes back, or Plaid does not reach an account at all, you enter the value by hand and it counts towards your net worth like any other account.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can LasagnaFi move my money?</summary>
        <p>No. The connection Plaid opens is read only, so nothing here can make a payment or a transfer. Moving money is something you do at your own bank.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Do you see my bank password?</summary>
        <p>No. The bank login happens in a window Plaid opens, so the password does not reach us.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How does LasagnaFi use AI?</summary>
        <p>A model writes the explanation behind an action, and the reply when you ask about it in chat. Chat answers from your own accounts and transactions rather than from general knowledge. Ways to spend less are found by code reading your transactions, and the step each one asks you to take comes from a fixed list rather than from a model. It is not allowed to quote a price or a rate for another company.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What does the AI see?</summary>
        <p>Your balances, rates, dates and transaction descriptions. It does not see your name, your email, your account numbers, or the names on your accounts. Two things are exceptions, because they cannot work any other way: a document you upload, and text you paste in to import.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What about a tax document I upload?</summary>
        <p>A photo or PDF cannot be anonymized. Anything printed on it, including your name and your Social Security number, is visible to the model that reads it. We delete the file once it has been read, and keep the figures from it.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Who else gets my data?</summary>
        <p>The services that run the app: Plaid for the account connection, WorkOS for sign-in, Stripe for payment, Google Cloud for the servers, OpenRouter for the AI models, and Umami for anonymous usage counts. Our privacy policy has the current list. No advertiser is on it, and nothing is sold.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What happens when I delete my account?</summary>
        <p>The account owner has a Delete account button in Settings. It cancels any subscription, disconnects your banks at Plaid, and removes your accounts, transactions, chat history and uploaded figures. Backups roll off after that, and Plaid and Stripe keep their own records under their own policies.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is this financial advice?</summary>
        <p>No. LasagnaFi is not a registered investment advisor, and nothing in it is financial, investment, tax or legal advice. For a decision that matters, talk to a licensed professional.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Does the free plan run out?</summary>
        <p>No, it is not a trial. If you connect more institutions than your plan covers, the ones past the limit keep their last known balance instead of disappearing, and they update again when you upgrade. Accounts you enter by hand do not use up a slot.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is there an app for my phone?</summary>
        <p>The hosted app runs in your phone's browser, so there is nothing to install.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can I run it myself?</summary>
        <p>Yes. The app is MIT licensed on GitHub and runs on Docker. You supply your own Plaid and AI keys.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
